From: =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=A9ven=20Car?= <meven@kde.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 09:20:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: keep a popup in place when it is resized

A popup with no parent control is placed through an anchor rectangle one
pixel wide, sitting at the position the window was given. The anchor edge
was the top right corner, which is one pixel to the right of that position.
The compositor placed the popup there, the client stored the answer as its
geometry, and the next positioner was built from that geometry, so every
resize moved the popup one pixel further right. A popup which changes size
while it is open, such as a menu whose entries grow wider, moved further
right on every change.

Anchor to the top left corner of that rectangle instead. The popup is then
placed on the position it was given, and the next positioner asks for that
same position.

The mock compositor now records what a positioner asks for, so the test can
show a popup, grant the position it asked for, resize it, and check that it
asks to stay where it is.

See: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=525054

